<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Erzincan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Erzincan is a city in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>, in a fertile plain surrounded by mountains. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the seat of the Mengujekid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> and later of the Eretnids and local emirs before passing to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. It lies on a major fault line and has been destroyed by earthquakes, notably in 1939, when more than 30,000 people died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/erzincan.jpg" alt="Erzincan" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Erzincann · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Erzincanmerkezi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
